The `main` function prompts the user to enter a value for `n`, then calls the `fibonacci` function with that value and prints the result.

Note that this implementation is not very efficient for large values of `n`, as it involves a lot of redundant calculations due to the recursive calls. A more efficient approach would be to use dynamic programming to store the results of previous calculations and avoid recomputing them.

